              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To convert your grade to a percentage, it depends on what kind of grade you are starting with. \n\nIf you want me to calculate it for you, **just reply with your grade (e.g., \"17 out of 23\" or \"B+\") and I will calculate it instantly!**\n\nOtherwise, you can use the guides, formulas, and charts below to convert your grades:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Points to Percentage (e.g., Test Scores)\nIf you have a score (like 18 out of 25) and want to find the percentage, use this simple formula:\n\n$$\\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Your Score}}{\\text{Total Possible Points}} \\right) \\times 100$$\n\n*   **Example:** You got **37** out of **45** points.\n    *   $37 \\div 45 = 0.8222$\n    *   $0.8222 \\times 100 =$ **$82.2\\%$** (which is a **B** or **B-** depending on your school's scale).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Letter Grade to Percentage Chart\nMost schools in the US use a standard 4.0 GPA and percentage scale. *Note: Exact percentage ranges can vary by school or teacher.*\n\n| Letter Grade | Percentage Range | GPA (4.0 Scale) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **A+** | 97% \u2013 100% | 4.0 |\n| **A** | 93% \u2013 96% | 4.0 |\n| **A-** | 90% \u2013 92% | 3.7 |\n| **B+** | 87% \u2013 89% | 3.3 |\n| **B** | 83% \u2013 86% | 3.0 |\n| **B-** | 80% \u2013 82% | 2.7 |\n| **C+** | 77% \u2013 79% | 2.3 |\n| **C** | 73% \u2013 76% | 2.0 |\n| **C-** | 70% \u2013 72% | 1.7 |\n| **D+** | 67% \u2013 69% | 1.3 |\n| **D** | 65% \u2013 66% | 1.0 |\n| **F** | Below 65% | 0.0 |\n\n---\n\n### 3. GPA to Percentage\nIf you have a GPA on a **4.0 scale** and want to find the equivalent percentage, you can use this standard conversion formula:\n\n$$\\text{Percentage} = (\\text{GPA} \\times 20) + 20$$\n\n*   **Example:** A **3.5 GPA**\n    *   $(3.5 \\times 20) + 20 = 70 + 20 =$ **$90\\%$**\n\n*(Note: Some schools use a direct linear conversion, $\\text{GPA} \\div 4.0 \\times 100$, where a 3.0 GPA is a 75%. Check with your school's handbook to see which method they use.)*\n\n---\n\n### 4. Create Your Own Desktop Calculator\nIf you want an actual interactive calculator on your computer, you can copy the code below, paste it into Notepad, save the file as `calculator.html`, and double-click it to open it in any web browser:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>Grade to Percentage Calculator</title>\n    <style>\n        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 50px; background-color: #f4f4f9; text-align: center;}\n        .card { background: white; padding: 30px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); display: inline-block; }\n        input { padding: 10px; font-size: 16px; width: 80px; margin: 10px; border-radius: 5px; border: 1px solid #ccc; text-align: center; }\n        button { padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; background-color: #007BFF; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; }\n        button:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }\n        #result { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; color: #333; }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Grade to Percentage Calculator</h2>\n        <input type=\"number\" id=\"score\" placeholder=\"Score\"> \n        / \n        <input type=\"number\" id=\"total\" placeholder=\"Total\">\n        <br><br>\n        <button onclick=\"calculate()\">Calculate</button>\n        <div id=\"result\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        function calculate() {\n            var score = parseFloat(document.getElementById('score').value);\n            var total = parseFloat(document.getElementById('total').value);\n            if (isNaN(score) || isNaN(total) || total === 0) {\n                document.getElementById('result').innerText = \"Please enter valid numbers.\";\n                return;\n            }\n            var percentage = (score / total) * 100;\n            document.getElementById('result').innerText = \"Percentage: \" + percentage.toFixed(2) + \"%\";\n        }\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```",
